 "text": "Hello, how are you holding up? A sketch is a quick drawing done in one sitting, usually humorous or playful, while a study is a more detailed and serious piece done from real life or a model. Kind of, yes. It's the next step up from drawing what you see in a book or gallery. That's the time for studies. Pick few key features and really study them. Clouds are tough. Try plining them first, then filling in. Or start with thick lines on one side and detailing them up. The simple versus detailed thing. Studies usually pick few key features and really study them. A sketch is usually quick and rough to look like you didn't put any thought into it. Enjoy process, drawing is more about the journey than the destination.",
